<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Smarter Workflows – Benchmarks</title><link>https://circleci-labs.github.io/smarter-workflows/docs/benchmarks/</link><description>Recent content in Benchmarks on Smarter Workflows</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-US</language><atom:link href="https://circleci-labs.github.io/smarter-workflows/docs/benchmarks/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Benchmarks</title><link>https://circleci-labs.github.io/smarter-workflows/docs/benchmarks/benchmarks/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://circleci-labs.github.io/smarter-workflows/docs/benchmarks/benchmarks/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;Measured results for v0.1: real CircleCI pipelines for job selection, a replay of this repository&amp;rsquo;s history against today&amp;rsquo;s map, and synthetic workloads for planner and trace timing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="method"&gt;Method&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="method"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#method" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End to end&lt;/strong&gt; — &lt;code&gt;scripts/e2e/run-scenarios.sh&lt;/code&gt; pushes a one-commit branch per scenario, waits for the setup workflow and the continued workflow, and compares the jobs that ran with the expected set. Each scenario runs three times on the same base commit; medians use the per-target full-run scenarios as the baseline. Details: &lt;a href="https://circleci-labs.github.io/smarter-workflows/docs/validation/#end-to-end-scenarios"&gt;Validation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backtest&lt;/strong&gt; — &lt;code&gt;circleci-smarter backtest&lt;/code&gt; replays a JSON history file in select mode with a fixed impact map. Details: &lt;a href="https://circleci-labs.github.io/smarter-workflows/docs/benchmarks/benchmarks-backtest/"&gt;Backtest&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance&lt;/strong&gt; — Go &lt;code&gt;testing.B&lt;/code&gt; benchmarks and &lt;code&gt;scripts/bench/perf.sh&lt;/code&gt; on generated configs and temporary git repos. Details: &lt;a href="https://circleci-labs.github.io/smarter-workflows/docs/benchmarks/benchmarks-perf/"&gt;Performance benchmarks&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="end-to-end-savings"&gt;End-to-end savings&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="end-to-end-savings"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#end-to-end-savings" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job seconds&lt;/strong&gt; are the sum of each job&amp;rsquo;s reported run time in the continued workflow (including &lt;code&gt;smarter-gate&lt;/code&gt;). They are a stand-in for compute time, not credits: resource class affects credits, and queue time is excluded. On the &lt;a href="https://circleci-labs.github.io/smarter-workflows/docs/get-started/demo/"&gt;demo monorepo&lt;/a&gt;, the two &lt;code&gt;worker-test&lt;/code&gt; matrix jobs always run in v0.1, so they appear in every row below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Median job seconds per scenario (three runs each, base commit on main, 2026-11-15). Full-run medians: &lt;strong&gt;154 s&lt;/strong&gt; (demo, 13 jobs) and &lt;strong&gt;537 s&lt;/strong&gt; (this repository, 8 jobs).&lt;/p&gt;
